WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:12.733
Bottom line: Microsoft is a portfolio, not one system; first map the need to Windows, Microsoft 365, Azure or Copilot, then verify entitlements early.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:21.000
Start with Windows when the decision is the PC experience: devices, desktop, apps and user productivity.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.400
It anchors the endpoint for users, not every cloud service.

00:00:25.967 --> 00:00:35.033
Use Microsoft 365 when the need is everyday work: Office apps, email, files, meetings, sharing and collaboration.

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:39.267
It packages work services, not custom infrastructure.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:46.500
Use Azure when applications need cloud services: compute, storage, data and AI categories.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.367
It is the builder layer for apps and managed resources for teams.

00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:58.133
Treat Copilot as AI assistance that sits inside selected workflows and licenses.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:04.667
Confirm access, grounding, service availability and subscription before commitments.
